        "original_id": "335222be-544f-5873-b3c3-41aa59a66bc1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sidney Olcott, Denis Villeneuve, Gene Gauntier\n- Works: From the Manger to the Cross, Maelström, Polytechnique, Incendies, Enemy\n- Awards: Canadian Screen Award, Genie Award\n- Roles: film producer, director, actor, screenwriter, writer\n\nFacts:\n- Sidney Olcott was born on September 20, 1872, and died on December 16, 1949.\n- Sidney Olcott was a Canadian-born film producer, director, actor, and screenwriter.\n- From the Manger to the Cross was directed by Sidney Olcott, who also appeared in the film.\n- Gene Gauntier wrote the script for From the Manger to the Cross and portrayed the Virgin Mary in the film.\n- Denis Villeneuve was born on October 3, 1967, and is a French Canadian film director and writer.\n- Denis Villeneuve received the Canadian Screen Award, formerly called the Genie Award, for Best Direction for Maelström in 2001, Polytechnique in 2010, Incendies in 2011, and Enemy in 2013.",
